            <ArticleTitle>[Neuro-physiological mechanisms involved in the transmission of pain].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>22-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The author analyzes the importance of pain as a defense mechanism against a noxious stimulus; its sensory-discriminatory, affective-emotional, cognitive and behavior components; and how the transmission of pain impulses by means of peripheral receptors occur; neuronal ways of conduction; and the reception and interpretation of pain. The author also states the objectives nurses have in treating pain.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
